# Topic: Rocks
T:Rocks
T:Reference
T:Category
T:Science
T:------------
T:What it is
T:In geology,
T:a rock is
T:any
T:naturally
T:occurring
T:solid mass
T:or aggregate
T:of minerals
T:or
T:mineraloid
T:matter. It
T:is
T:categorized
T:by the
T:minerals
T:included,
T:its chemical
T:composition,
T:and the way
T:in which it
T:is formed.
T:Rocks form
T:the Earth's
T:outer solid
T:layer, the
T:crust, and
T:most of its
T:interior,
T:except for
T:the liquid
T:outer core
T:and pockets
T:of magma in
T:the
T:asthenosphe.
T:The study of
T:rocks
T:involves
T:multiple
T:subdisciplin
T:of geology,
T:including
T:petrology
T:and
T:mineralogy.
T:It may be
T:limited to
T:rocks found
T:on Earth, or
T:it may
T:include
T:planetary
T:geology that
T:studies the
T:rocks of
T:other
T:celestial
T:objects.
